#
# SSH keys allowed to sign release tags (slice 30 §11). The release workflow verifies every
# v* tag against the copy of this file on main; a tag signed by any other key, or not signed,
# stops the release before anything is built. GPG keys go in .github/release-keys.asc instead.
#
# One line per key, the same keys as in MAINTAINERS.md. Adding or removing a key is a reviewed
# pull request. Format (see "ALLOWED SIGNERS" in `man ssh-keygen`):
#
#   you@example.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...
#
# Empty until the release manager adds their key (docs/stores.md, "Signing keys"); until then
# every release tag is refused.
